FORTRESS FILLOMINO:

• Divide the grid into orthogonally connected regions and fill each cell with a number (not necessarily single-digit) showing the number of cells in the region to which it belongs;

• Each region must be either strictly larger than all of its orthogonal neighbors or strictly smaller than all of its orthogonal neighbors;

• For answer check, fill cells with the ones digit of each region's size.

CHOCO BANANA:

• Each fillomino region is either a Choco or a Banana;

• A Choco region is rectangular in shape and is not orthogonally adjacent to any other Choco region;

• A Banana region is non-rectangular in shape and is not orthogonally adjacent to any other Banana regions.

THERMOMETER:

• Numbers along a grey thermometer strictly increase from bulb to tip.
